{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[],"claim_ids":[],"created_at":"2026-09-14T01:37:43Z","created_by_operation":"op_f839a6060e9a42d3a170c71f3fe3b8f4","id":"pg_773b8caa741857bcb1eb2fbc8756dfee","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/bhouston-mycoder-docs-prompt-tips-md-774e068e5dae-2fbc8756dfee.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_294c82f9b71d56ed9c79b504b78d1d9d"],"title":"bhouston/mycoder/docs/prompt-tips.md @ 774e068e5dae","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:37:43Z","updated_by_operation":"op_f839a6060e9a42d3a170c71f3fe3b8f4"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_811cf508b2c3e73d3cce56d7d48563df557bc2aecbb3f626831628140d6d4194"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Users can define custom CLI commands in mycoder.config.js with description, args, and an execute function returning a prompt string; execute may be asynchronous, and custom commands cannot override built-ins."}],"claim_ids":["clm_811cf508b2c3e73d3cce56d7d48563df557bc2aecbb3f626831628140d6d4194"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T01:37:43Z","created_by_operation":"op_f839a6060e9a42d3a170c71f3fe3b8f4","id":"pg_9388e64b122a5eba83f3df9ddb0e1d72","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/bhouston-mycoder-docs-custom-commands-md-774e068e5dae-df9ddb0e1d72.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_f7392cd31ea15908b0269463213fa9d5"],"title":"bhouston/mycoder/docs/custom-commands.md @ 774e068e5dae","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:37:43Z","updated_by_operation":"op_f839a6060e9a42d3a170c71f3fe3b8f4"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_13727861b09edf775d51e1eeed662317e425bd2f693da1590234cbb99a45e2b0"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"MyCoder is a command-line interface for AI-powered coding tasks, installable globally via npm."},{"claim_ids":["clm_147e89f771065bcc89af4309e8e6c133022464e0e817f742b562d29e6e2bbf6f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Configuration is resolved from multiple locations in precedence order (project-root mycoder.config.js variants, .mycoder.rc, package.json 'mycoder' field, XDG user config) and supports many file formats; CLI arguments override config-file settings."},{"claim_ids":["clm_5315fed80e403e031415a87be7d61065f669cdd77f6b123459b8e3d1e044358e"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The repository is a monorepo with packages for the CLI (mycoder), the agent module (mycoder-agent), and a documentation website (mycoder-docs)."},{"claim_ids":["clm_7dbd129df1bbcaccdda3283960c665d4fb75adcc50e55ffb18ec1923991db512"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: contributors clone the repo, run pnpm install/build/test/commit, and releases follow Conventional Commits with an automated CI/CD pipeline that versions, generates a changelog, creates a GitHub Release, tags, and publishes to NPM after PR review and merge to main."},{"claim_ids":["clm_8d4a16d014f6a851e63fb00ead2cbe9f5c82a76b88cbef174bf913669e57d5db"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The agent leverages Anthropic's Claude, OpenAI models, and Ollama, and uses Playwright for browser automation, which normally requires separate browser installation."},{"claim_ids":["clm_8fe42009510d3705d71eabb048e566865ff15528ab82f674c9c1c9f7ede94c0b"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The CLI supports interactive mode (-i), prompt arguments, prompt files (-f), an --interactive correction mode, and flags like --userPrompt false and --upgradeCheck false for automated runs."},{"claim_ids":["clm_b21356fc24fb5c7571891599b88c9be6e6559adc28e51fbfafcacf4de4c3f53f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"MyCoder supports Model Context Protocol (MCP) server configuration with named servers, bearer auth, default resources, and default tools, plus a GitHub mode for working with issues and PRs including /mycoder comment commands."},{"claim_ids":["clm_bf5de17e4dedac00ffd37fe9c375666165e1cc9882790d81103535113734962e"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"MyCoder can spawn sub-agents for concurrent task processing, and status updates report active sub-agents, shell processes, and browser sessions."},{"claim_ids":["clm_eb8936d9ebfd494ca25f96b9b5b51bf201eec1762595c9c87890db0d1f92d7ec"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A system browser detection feature lets MyCoder use installed Chrome, Edge, Firefox and other browsers on Windows, macOS, and Linux, falling back to Playwright's bundled browsers when none is found."},{"claim_ids":["clm_fc9ecd126a7b8c1590632529267490703f00ea2de01aa20141f8960d264b2723"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"With --interactive, users can press Ctrl+M during execution to send corrections to the running agent, which incorporates them into its decision-making; this can also be enabled via an 'interactive: true' config option."}],"claim_ids":["clm_13727861b09edf775d51e1eeed662317e425bd2f693da1590234cbb99a45e2b0","clm_147e89f771065bcc89af4309e8e6c133022464e0e817f742b562d29e6e2bbf6f","clm_5315fed80e403e031415a87be7d61065f669cdd77f6b123459b8e3d1e044358e","clm_7dbd129df1bbcaccdda3283960c665d4fb75adcc50e55ffb18ec1923991db512","clm_8d4a16d014f6a851e63fb00ead2cbe9f5c82a76b88cbef174bf913669e57d5db","clm_8fe42009510d3705d71eabb048e566865ff15528ab82f674c9c1c9f7ede94c0b","clm_b21356fc24fb5c7571891599b88c9be6e6559adc28e51fbfafcacf4de4c3f53f","clm_bf5de17e4dedac00ffd37fe9c375666165e1cc9882790d81103535113734962e","clm_eb8936d9ebfd494ca25f96b9b5b51bf201eec1762595c9c87890db0d1f92d7ec","clm_fc9ecd126a7b8c1590632529267490703f00ea2de01aa20141f8960d264b2723"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T01:37:43Z","created_by_operation":"op_f839a6060e9a42d3a170c71f3fe3b8f4","id":"pg_d93ef11e99fe5e9e8b79115972a938f2","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/bhouston-mycoder-readme-md-774e068e5dae-115972a938f2.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_f04ea5b7b3615a67bd10d659bf81662c"],"title":"bhouston/mycoder/README.md @ 774e068e5dae","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:37:43Z","updated_by_operation":"op_f839a6060e9a42d3a170c71f3fe3b8f4"}
